--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Development material that ships with the plugin, on purpose
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two files in this repository are development material rather than game code,
and a reviewer is right to ask why an installed plugin carries them. Both are
kept deliberately, because docs/plan.md requires them in-tree under
"Prerequisites before kicking it off", and both are revisited at milestone M6
when the submission commit is tagged.

.claude/skills/gauntlet-loop/   (about 8 KB)
    Prerequisite 4: "The gauntlet-loop skill is copied into the repository at
    .claude/skills/gauntlet-loop/." It describes the development workflow this
    repository is built with. The Omarchy shell never loads it, it is not
    referenced by manifest.json or by any QML file, and it is attributed above.
    It is 8 KB of text on the installing machine and it changes nothing about
    what the plugin does. Alternative considered and rejected for now: moving
    the skill to a separate repository, which would break the prerequisite the
    build plan states.

The design mock             (1.78 MB)
    Prerequisite 3: "these files are committed under docs/: design.md,
    plan.md, garage-room-mock.png (Sol's Garage Room image), environment.md."
    That is why the file travels with the design documents that cite it, and
    docs/design.md:229 states that the invite code and the friend badges are
    absent from the solo layout. It is the largest file in the repository.
    The three sentences that describe it are fixed strings in
    src/tools/check-readme.ts, and README.md carries them verbatim too:

    `docs/garage-room-mock.png` is a design mock of the future multiplayer
    lobby: an invite code, four named children, ready toggles and APPROVED
    FRIEND / DEVICE VERIFIED badges, none of which exists in this plugin,
    which is solo and offline. Only the kart stall on its left, the body,
    paint and number pickers, is the reference the solo garage will be built
    against. It is not a screenshot of this plugin and must never be used as
    its preview.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Game assets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

assets/karts/<body>/<paint>.png, assets/karts/<body>/meta.json,
assets/karts/manifest.json
    The car sprite sheets: six bodies (coupe, hatch, wedge, saloon, buggy,
    pickup) in eight paints, two cameras, eight yaws and three scales each.
    Original work, generated by this repository's own scripts and nothing
    else: src/tools/bake-cars.py builds each body from primitives in Blender
    (run headless, `blender -b`; no .blend file exists) and src/tools/pxart.py
    reduces the renders to the pixel grid and palette. `npm run sprites`
    regenerates every file byte for byte and `npm run check:sprites` verifies
    the committed files against manifest.json's SHA-256 records. No third-party
    model, texture, font or photograph is involved; the reference image the
    style was judged against, docs/golden-hour-car.png, is not sampled or
    traced. Licence: MIT, with the rest of the repository.

Everything else under assets/ is still empty (props/, cards/, sfx/), and
shaders/ holds no shader source. As artwork, sound and shaders land they are
recorded here, one entry per source, giving the title, the author, the
licence, and the URL it came from. The project's rule for accepting an asset
is: original work, or CC0, or a licence at least as permissive as MIT, with
attribution recorded here whether or not the licence demands it.

